ary, distinct public addresses. The shared private address never left either home, so it never collides."],[10120,"Now the phone in home A sends, from its own private address, 192.168.1.23."],[12010,"Same public address, 203.0.113.7, the whole home shares it. The router hands this conversation a different port, and the table is what tells each reply apart."],[14740,"The server sees two ordinary, distinct public addresses. The shared private address never left either home, so it never collides."]]}